 Denmark from 1979 to 1992. In Danish with English abstract</article-title><source>Ugeskr Laeger</source><year>1998</year><volume>160</volume><fpage>7118</fpage><lpage>7121</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9850616</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bj&#x000f8;rk</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Vinther-Larsen</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Thygesen</surname><given-names>LC</given-names></name><name><surname>Johansen</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Gr&#x000f8;nb&#x000e6;k</surname><given-names>MN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Alcohol consumption by middle-aged and elderly Danes from 1987 to 2003. In Danish with English abstract</article-title><source>Ugeskr Laeger</source><year>2006</year><volume>168</volume><fpage>3317</fpage><lpage>3321</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17032597</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stokkeland</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Brandt</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Ekbom</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Hultcrantz</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Improved prognosis for patients hospitalized with esophageal varices in Sweden 1969&#x02013;2002</article-title><source>Hepatology</source><year>2006</year><volume>43</volume><fpage>500</fpage><lpage>505</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16496319</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/hep.21089</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Talwalkar</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Kamath</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Influence of recent advances in medical management on clinical outcomes of cirrhosis</article-title><source>Mayo Clin Proc</source><year>2005</year><volume>80</volume><fpage>1501</fpage><lpage>1508</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16295030</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Almdal</surname><given-names>TP</given-names></name><name><surname>S&#x000f8;rensen</surname><given-names>TI</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Incidence of parenchymal liver diseases in Denmark, 1981 to 1985: analysis of hospitalization registry data</article-title><source>Hepatology</source><year>1991</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>650</fpage><lpage>655</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2010159</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Frank</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>When an entire country is a cohort</article-title><source>Science</source><year>2000</year><volume>287</volume><fpage>2398</fpage><lpage>2399</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10766613</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1126/science.287.5462.2398</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Andersen</surname><given-names>TF</given-names></name><name><surname>Madsen</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>J&#x000f8;rgensen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Mellemkj&#x000e6;r</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Olsen</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Danish National Hospital Register. A valuable source of data for modern health sciences</article-title><source>Dan Med Bull</source><year>1999</year><volume>46</volume><fpage>263</fpage><lpage>268</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10421985</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id